          'Older walk-ups near the restaurant streets have a half-landing and a door that opens outward into the stair. A fridge has to be turned on that landing, not slid. If the building has no lift, say the floor number plainly. Third floor and fifth floor are different jobs in Barsha even when the appliance is the same. We protect the tiled edges. We do not leave the old unit on the landing for “someone” to finish. If the shop below is open, we wait for a gap rather than blocking their door with a trolley. Tell us the shop hours if you know them. A lunchtime lull is often the cleanest gap on those restaurant streets, and it is worth naming when you book so the crew is not queued behind a delivery at the busiest hour.'
